    "post_update_notes": "Fixes the actual root cause behind the BackupRun error, confirmed from your log file. A database restore (used to undo a failed update) replays each table as drop-then-recreate, and the backup system's own bookkeeping tables were included in that \u2014 so a failed update's automatic rollback could wipe out a fresh retry's in-progress backup record. Those bookkeeping tables are now permanently excluded from every backup/restore, so this can't happen again. Also fixed 6 migrations from v1.0.16 that weren't safe to re-run after an interrupted update (the same underlying cause as the earlier admin_sessions/FULLTEXT-index errors) \u2014 all are now idempotent. If you're on 1.0.15, update straight to this version.",
